node_modules/
package-lock.json

.crawler/

# Build output. Generated from the sources in sources.json by build.mjs, and
# built fresh by CI on every push to main (.github/workflows/deploy.yml), which
# then uploads it to the site. Deliberately NOT tracked: when it was, CI pushed
# a "Build: recompile dist/" commit after every push, which landed on top of
# whatever you were doing and turned the next push into a merge.
#
# Run ./build.sh after editing anything under libControl/ to refresh your local
# copy — a fresh clone has no dist/ until you do.
#
# THE TWO EXCEPTIONS ARE dist/gui.js AND dist/app.js, AND THEY ARE TRACKED FOR
# THE REASON KAD'S dist IS. APK:OS does not carry effects of its own:
# Mixer/dsp/load-sampler-gui.js loads the FACEPLATES out of this folder, and
# .apk.scripts/deploy.py publishes it, so a checkout without gui.js is nine
# Audio & DSP windows drawing "has no engine in this window" — which is what
# apk.audio drew until 2026-09-06. dist/app.js is this app's OWN bundle, loaded
# by its own index.html, and PLAN-364.01 put that page on the site: untracked,
# it is the Launch Pad's `Sampler & Play` and `Sound Library` drawing a 404.
# CI cannot recompile either into a commit here: nothing in .github/workflows/
# builds this app, and the loop the paragraph above remembers was closed
# anyway when OA_BUILD_VERSION stopped reading the clock and started reading
# the last commit that touched a source. `node build.mjs --check` is what
# holds both committed bundles to those sources; `check.sh sampler` runs it.
#
# dist/precache.json stays untracked. It is generated too, but --check does not
# gate it, and sw.js already falls back to a four-entry shell list when the
# fetch 404s — so an unpublished manifest degrades instead of lying.
/dist/*
!/dist/gui.js
!/dist/app.js
